window.PLACETYPE_DOCS_SEARCH = [{"slug":"index","title":"Overview","text":"A visual algorithm guide · version 0.1.2 From place observations to defensible economic categories. PlaceType PH classifies canonical establishments using Philippine statistical taxonomies. This guide shows exactly how source labels, reviewed rules, hierarchy constraints, uncertainty, institution evidence, and input–output correspondence become auditable results. Follow a worked example → Run the package 3 distinct statistical classification systems 346 bundled reviewed PSIC Rev. 5 rules 178 specialized advisory activity rules What the package does PlaceType PH sits after OpenPlaces PH , which supplies one canonical record per reconciled place. PlaceType PH does not repeat the geometric or name-based record linkage upstream. It interprets the source evidence attached to those records and maps it to the official hierarchy, stopping at a defensible level rather than inventing a more specific category. Figure 1 — Conceptual pipeline. Source and institutional evidence inform decisions, but candidate-only information does not silently become an accepted classification. The three taxonomies answer different questions : Scheme What is classified Boundary PSIC Rev. 5 The establishment's principal economic activity A parent code may be the best supported answer. PCPC 2002 Product and service categories A place-only label is a potential product/service family , not its complete output basket. PSCC 2022 Traded commodities A shop name is not proof of a particular traded commodity. Explicit commodity evidence or a confirmed mapping is required. The source is not a probability model. A match to a reviewed category is a rule assertion; two matching labels may derive from one provider; a code set is not proof of a specific production technology. These distinctions are preserved in outputs and audit fields. Read this like an implementation specification The documentation follows the two complementary styles of a visual worked derivation and a system-design manual: start with a small example, then inspect every transformation, input contract, fallback, status, implementation file, and limiting assumption. It is organized into chapters rather than one unsearchable README. 01 Worked example Trace a pharmacy, a disputed place, and an administrative office through actual decision rules. 02 Evidence triangulation Why source dependence, corroboration, and contradictory annotations matter. 03 Hierarchy & fusion Exact subtree intersections, sibling backoff, unions and conflicts without forced leaves. 04 Cross-taxonomy review Learn what the bounded peer-context recheck can and cannot legitimately infer. 05 Institutional evidence Separate an institution's activity from ownership and from derived I–O industries. 06 Reproducibility Taxonomy versions, packaged rules, fingerprints, caches, and selective invalidation. What “triangulation” means here PlaceType PH does not use geometric triangulation (Delaunay or otherwise). Its triangulation is semantic : comparing source annotations with dependency-aware fusion and separately checking proposals against other taxonomies in a bounded diagnostic pass. The latter is advisory, not an official statistical concordance. See source triangulation and cross-taxonomy rechecking . Not an accuracy certificate All tests passing, a complete reference hierarchy, a reviewed rule inventory, or a singleton I–O candidate set do not establish ground-truth classification accuracy. The [evaluation](evaluation.html) chapter explains the necessary adjudicated benchmark and what the current package reports. How to navigate Start with Quickstart for an executable example; then read Architecture , Source evidence , and Tree fusion to understand the decision engine. The Design decision register distinguishes standard statistical ideas from package-specific choices and known fallbacks. The API and CLI and Outputs chapters are references for implementation and downstream work. Source: Repository · README · architecture note .","headings":["What the package does","Read this like an implementation specification","What “triangulation” means here","How to navigate"]},{"slug":"getting-started","title":"Quickstart","text":"Quickstart Install the package, verify taxonomy inputs, classify an existing OpenPlaces Parquet, and inspect the outputs. No hosted model is required for the deterministic baseline. Prerequisites Python 3.11–3.13 is covered by the repository's current CI matrix; the project declares Python 3.11 or newer. A valid OpenPlaces PH canonical_pois.parquet , containing unique non-null canonical_id and at least one supported semantic source field. Normalized taxonomy files under reference/ or source workbooks/API access to create them. The repository includes normalized taxonomy assets, but the operator should validate versions before analytical use. Install and confirm the environment $ErrorActionPreference = \"Stop\" cd \"$HOME\\Documents\\GitHub\\placetype-ph\" conda env update -f environment.yml --prune if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Conda environment update failed\" } conda activate placetype-ph python -m pip install -e \".[dev]\" if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Editable install failed\" } placetype version if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Version check failed\" } python -m ruff check . if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Lint failed\" } python -m pytest -q if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Tests failed\" } Expected package version for this guide: 0.1.2 . The official taxonomy files need their own validation; a successful package installation does not guarantee the supplied statistical references are complete. Inspect the inputs first $places = \"..\\openplaces-ph\\data\\output\\areas_iloilo\\canonical_pois.parquet\" if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $places -PathType Leaf)) { throw \"OpenPlaces input missing\" } placetype inspect $places --top 30 if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Inspect failed\" } placetype taxonomy validate reference\\psic_rev5\\nodes.parquet --strict-levels --strict-structure if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Taxonomy validation failed\" } If a taxonomy is absent, use placetype taxonomy diagnose psic before placetype taxonomy fetch psic ; PCPC's official API may require a PSA token. See Taxonomy integrity . Run the reviewed PSIC baseline placetype classify $places ` --schemes psic --llm none ` --output-dir output\\iloilo-reviewed if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Reviewed classification failed\" } The default PSIC Rev. 5 run includes the 346 bundled accepted mappings and the conservative operational rules. It does not call an LLM. A custom reviewed crosswalk may be supplied with repeated --crosswalk arguments. Conflicting exact keys are validation errors; they do not silently override the packaged rules. Make a controlled legacy comparison placetype classify $places ` --schemes psic --llm none --no-reviewed-psic ` --output-dir output\\iloilo-legacy if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Legacy comparison failed\" } This disables the newly introduced reviewed-PSIC policy and packaged mappings without disabling explicitly supplied crosswalks or earlier classifier rules. Keep the taxonomy, input file, and optional user crosswalk constant for a meaningful comparison; the result is not a causal estimate of classification quality. Or use the complete Express workflow placetype express $places --workers 1 if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Express run failed\" } Express builds a joint crosswalk, runs bounded cross-taxonomy rechecks, classifies selected schemes, and exports a QGIS-ready GeoParquet. Important: Express promotes unchecked machine suggestions by default and labels them AUTO_ACCEPTED_UNCHECKED . For a conservative gate, add --no-promote-unchecked ; this can result in little coverage on a cold start. See Express . Verify the outputs A classify run writes entity_classifications.parquet , classified_pois.parquet , and run.json . The GeoParquet output of express is a separate compact layer; it is not a replacement for the audit-rich classification table. Check Outputs for the schema and interpretation rules. To evaluate classifications you need independently adjudicated gold labels ; see Evaluation . A large number of assigned codes, by itself, is only coverage .","headings":["Prerequisites","Install and confirm the environment","Inspect the inputs first","Run the reviewed PSIC baseline","Make a controlled legacy comparison","Or use the complete Express workflow","Verify the outputs"]},{"slug":"architecture","title":"Architecture","text":"System architecture The core architecture is a separation of responsibilities: canonical place identity, statistical classification, auxiliary institutional evidence, and economic concordance are different layers with different proof obligations. System boundary Figure 1 — Classification begins with canonical entities. Upstream matching and downstream economic interpretation are not part of the primary PSIC code decision. Upstream: OpenPlaces PH supplies canonical IDs, linked provider names/categories, provenance, coordinates, and matching diagnostics. PlaceType PH neither merges nor splits those upstream entities. It may flag suspicious records ( REVIEW_ENTITY_MATCH ) when independent semantic evidence disagrees and matching-quality indicators are present. Classification core: openplaces.py produces typed evidence, crosswalk.py matches reviewed rules, fusion.py reasons over actual taxonomy parent edges, classifier.py applies eligibility and policy guards, and retrieval.py / traversal.py supply an optional model fallback. taxonomy.py holds the normalized official hierarchy. Joint review workflow: joint_crosswalk.py and suggest.py create worklists, preserve first-pass independence, and perform a bounded peer-context rerank. A peer recheck proposes no new code outside the first-pass candidate set. It is not a vote in the production fuse() algorithm. Additive enrichment: specialized activity, administrative, institutional and ownership modules attach review candidates and provenance. Default institutional identity enrichment may refine a separate I–O candidate projection where stringent gates are satisfied. It does not silently replace primary PSIC. Publication: pipeline.py produces audit-level and map-level Parquet, io_mapping.py attaches I–O sets, gis.py exports compact GeoParquet, and run.json records versions, fingerprints, and status counts. Modules and responsibilities Component Main modules Contract Official taxonomy taxonomy.py , taxonomy_import.py Nodes have explicit parents, levels, and versioned fingerprints. Canonical input openplaces.py Read canonical IDs and typed source fields; no new entity linkage. Reviewed decisions crosswalk.py , reviewed_psic.py Version-scoped exact/contains/regex rules; bundled 346 PSIC Rev. 5 rows. Evidence fusion fusion.py , eligibility.py Hierarchy intersection, dependency grouping, conflict or abstention. Optional decision fallback retrieval.py , traversal.py , cache.py Local TF-IDF, bounded taxonomy traversal, deterministic cache identity. Joint review joint_crosswalk.py , suggest.py Candidate worklist, first-pass control, diagnostic rerank. Institutional audit specialized/* Activity candidates, verified identity, conditional ownership enrichment. Economic candidate sets io_mapping.py , io80_resolver.py Rev. 5 → 2019 PSIC → 2018 I–O; never silently choose among candidates. Data products pipeline.py , gis.py , express.py Parquet, GeoParquet, manifest, cache-aware workflow. Three separate kinds of uncertainty Source uncertainty: two observed labels can be independent, correlated, broad, or contradictory. The source adapter and dependency groups make these distinctions explicit. Taxonomy uncertainty: one source label may support a subtree, a union of subtrees, or no category. The classifier stops at an ancestor or abstains where no unique defensible code exists. Economic correspondence uncertainty: even a valid PSIC code may map to more than one I–O industry, and bridging across statistical revisions may be provisional. Candidate sets and provenance are retained. These uncertainties cannot be collapsed into one confidence score without additional evidence and calibration. Decisions are typed; audits are additive ClassificationResult contains code , level , status , deciding_component , candidate_codes , evidence_sources , flags , audit , and depth metadata. Specialized enrichment attaches separate columns rather than silently modifying those fields. A SourceEvidence record stores source , category , name , dependency_group , and an optional reviewed mapping . The core distinction is accepted rule vs candidate . A high lexical score, registry name similarity, or recheck stability is not equivalent to human review or verified identity. Method lineage and traceability The taxonomy, hierarchical classifiers, TF-IDF retrieval, and constrained traversal use established structures/algorithms. Source-specific precision floors, independent sibling backoff, status vocabulary, promotion defaults, institutional matching gates, and I–O candidate narrowing are project policy . Their existence is documented in the design register , not presented as canonical statistical algorithms. Implementation: source tree · architecture specification .","headings":["System boundary","Modules and responsibilities","Three separate kinds of uncertainty","Decisions are typed; audits are additive","Method lineage and traceability"]},{"slug":"worked-example","title":"Worked example","text":"One example, three outcomes The easiest way to understand the system is to run a few small, explicitly illustrative records through its decision semantics. We will keep the same PSIC Rev. 5 hierarchy and vary only the evidence. About these examples The cases reflect rules and regression tests in the package (including pharmacy, banking, OSM compounds, and administrative offices). They are instructional traces, not measurements of actual Philippine places or model-inferred probabilities. To reproduce them, load the matching official taxonomy and reviewed crosswalk. Case A — Two compatible source categories An OpenPlaces entity contains overture_category = pharmacy and osm_category = shop=pharmacy . Suppose the corresponding accepted category assertions refer to PSIC 4772 in the loaded hierarchy. Figure 1 — Two independent providers can assert compatible taxonomic subtrees without needing a confidence-vote formula. The source adapter keeps OSM key=value and Overture label distinct; their dependency groups are independent unless provenance says otherwise. The crosswalk looks up each source's category, match type, and PSIC version. Fusion intersects the rooted subtrees. The surviving supported code is 4772; this is not an inferred deeper subclass. The output records the code, level, source list, status, and accepted-rule flags. When a single category supports only a division, the output must remain at that division unless another accepted assertion narrows it. Case B — Two sources, one lineage Suppose the record has Foursquare evidence and an Overture label explicitly recorded as derived from Foursquare ( overture_has_foursquare_provenance = true ). Both may describe banking. They are not two independent confirmations. Figure 2 — Dependence-aware corroboration. Two field values can constrain a subtree but are not two independent observations. If compatible, the records may narrow one another. If disjoint, the same-lineage conflict is flagged rather than converted into a fraudulent consensus. The worklist and run outputs preserve the provider identities. Case C — Disjoint economic activities A canonical entity combines osm_category = amenity=bank and overture_category = pharmacy . When accepted PSIC mappings point into unrelated branches, there is no defensible single principal activity. A forced subclass would silently discard a source contradiction. A common high-level ancestor may be too broad to explain either activity. The production result conservatively reports CONFLICT with candidate codes, or REVIEW_ENTITY_MATCH if the input carries entity-match warning indicators. This does not change OpenPlaces identity automatically; it asks the upstream matching process to be reviewed. Case D — Administrative function is not the service administered DepEd Schools Division Office may be annotated with amenity=school . A narrow administrative name can support 84120 , rather than treating the office as a school delivering education. But this correction is guarded: a reviewed exact category, unrelated activity evidence, or disjoint named rules can block it into review. A hospital office, a school itself, and a government agency may be related institutionally while carrying different principal economic activities . Public ownership is a separate question , and does not follow from PSIC 84120 alone. A practical comparison you can reproduce $places = \"..\\openplaces-ph\\data\\output\\areas_iloilo\\canonical_pois.parquet\" placetype classify $places --schemes psic --llm none --output-dir output\\reviewed if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Reviewed run failed\" } placetype classify $places --schemes psic --llm none --no-reviewed-psic --output-dir output\\legacy if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Legacy run failed\" } Compare code , status , flags and candidate_codes by canonical_id . More coded rows are not necessarily more correct; the adjudicated comparison in evaluation is required to assess correctness. Implementation & tests: test_reviewed_psic_transfer.py · classifier.py .","headings":["Case A — Two compatible source categories","Case B — Two sources, one lineage","Case C — Disjoint economic activities","Case D — Administrative function is not the service administered","A practical comparison you can reproduce"]},{"slug":"taxonomies","title":"Official taxonomies","text":"Official taxonomies & hierarchy integrity A taxonomy is not a bag of codes. PlaceType PH represents it as a verified rooted forest whose parent relationships, statistical revision, source metadata, and level ordering define every allowed classification and backoff. The three separate hierarchies Taxonomy Official hierarchy Interpretation PSIC Rev. 5 Section → division → group → class → subclass Principal economic activity of an establishment. PCPC 2002 Section → division → group → class → subclass → item A candidate product/service family based on place evidence. PSCC 2022 Chapter → heading → HS subheading → AHTN subheading → commodity Traded good; requires commodity evidence or confirmed crosswalk. The official PSIC Rev. 5 published structure is 22 sections, 88 divisions, 260 groups, 493 classes and 1,338 subclasses . PCPC and PSCC count baselines are deliberately not hard-coded without validating the actual official source. A tree, not numeric string truncation Figure 1 — Parent relationships govern ancestry. Section letters and cross-version recodings make numerical prefix slicing unsafe as a general algorithm. The functions taxonomy.ancestors(code) , taxonomy.children(code) , taxonomy.lca(codes) and taxonomy.path_from_root(code) use stored parent edges. A coarse classification SUBTREE(47) does not become a subclass just because one descendant is present in a partial extract; the evidence asserts the original root. Official sources and acquisition placetype taxonomy diagnose <scheme> inspects the statistical source before normalization; placetype taxonomy fetch <scheme> obtains or reuses the source and saves normalized nodes.parquet . PSIC Rev. 5 and PSCC 2022 use PSA spreadsheets. PCPC supports a PSA API requiring a token in relevant configurations. Refer to DATA_SOURCES.md for exact cited source URLs, licensing and recoding boundaries. The importer preserves code , level , title , parent_code , description/inclusions/exclusions and source identifiers. It rejects conflicting explicit parents and duplicate code definitions with incompatible identity. Source text for an official node titled “Other” is retained literally, even when “other” in a noisy POI label may be treated as missing evidence. Structural and completeness gates Missing top-level and parent nodes: strict normalization rejects a hierarchy that has the wrong branch attachment. Leading zero / invalid code morphology: report missing or malformed identifiers; do not silently coerce them into a plausible code. Explicit workbook schema: if a named column does not exist, fail rather than switch to a different parser interpretation. Duplicates: merge only consistent code identities; retain diagnostic counts for discarded or invalid rows. Hierarchy levels: --strict-levels checks completeness by level. --strict-structure checks known official structure when supported; --allow-orphan-nodes is a separate relaxation, not an override of everything. Version: a code under Rev. 5 cannot be silently interpreted as equivalent to the same string under PSIC 2019. A taxonomy fingerprint is recorded so an export can verify it is using the same classification tree as the original run. Reproducible commands placetype taxonomy diagnose psic if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Diagnosis failed\" } placetype taxonomy fetch psic if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Taxonomy fetch failed\" } placetype taxonomy validate reference\\psic_rev5\\nodes.parquet --strict-levels --strict-structure if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Taxonomy validation failed\" } Implementation: taxonomy.py · taxonomy_import.py .","headings":["The three separate hierarchies","A tree, not numeric string truncation","Official sources and acquisition","Structural and completeness gates","Reproducible commands"]},{"slug":"sources","title":"Source evidence","text":"Source evidence and provenance A canonical place can combine provider annotations from OSM, Overture and Foursquare. PlaceType PH turns those annotations into typed evidence without erasing provider identity, key/value meaning, or common origin. Input contract read_openplaces() reads Parquet, requires unique, non-null, non-blank canonical_id , and at least one supported source semantic field. Typical fields include osm_name , osm_category , overture_name , overture_category , fsq_name , fsq_category , and structured Overture primary/alternate/basic categories. Input coordinates and geometry are carried to the spatial summary as available; classification does not change them. Three provider streams Source Category handling Dependence / warning OSM Parse key=value primary assertions, not substring matches; ignore ancillary attributes for principal activity. Multiple substantive tags can describe disjoint activities and trigger review. Overture Preserve primary and alternate labels as dependent source statements; basic category is advisory context in the operational PSIC adapter. An Overture record may itself derive from Foursquare. Foursquare Preserve source-specific category hierarchy strings, rather than naively splitting category path text. Foursquare and FSQ-derived Overture are a single lineage. For example, shop=car and shop=carpet are different observed strings. An atm=yes auxiliary tag at a bank does not create a second principal banking/ATM activity. overture_basic_category = pharmacy alone is not accepted as a precise operational PSIC rule. Typed evidence is not a vote Every SourceEvidence contains a dependency_group . With explicit FSQ-derived provenance, Foursquare and Overture share fsq-lineage ; otherwise independent providers have separate groups. Categories and name rules from one provider remain dependent on the same upstream record. Agreement does not produce an invented confidence value, and multiple fields from one provider cannot be counted as independent corroboration. Name and category evidence A reviewed source_field=category mapping is a reusable category-to-hierarchy rule. A reviewed source_field=name mapping may be a high-precision chain or institution-specific assertion. If they are compatible they constrain the same root; if contradictory, the name precedence logic can preserve the narrower reviewed name rule while visibly flagging CROSSWALK_NAME_RULE_OVERRODE_CATEGORY . This is package policy, not a generic theorem about business names. When a precise reviewed name rule conflicts with a trusted category floor, the operational classifier retains counterevidence rather than manufacturing a single definitive code. Identity conflicts are returned upstream for review If independent categories disagree and the canonical record has match-risk indicators (transitive completion, large pair distance or low match score), the classifier can emit REVIEW_ENTITY_MATCH . It does not re-run the OpenPlaces matching algorithm or silently split one canonical ID into two. That distinction is critical: mismatched POI identity is an upstream data problem, not a reason to assume one establishment performs several activities. Untrusted input boundary Business names, descriptions, and provider tags are data , not instructions to a model. The optional traversal prompt explicitly tells the LLM not to obey embedded instructions. Provider normalization strips missing labels for matching but keeps official taxonomy titles intact. Implementation: openplaces.py · reviewed_psic.py .","headings":["Input contract","Three provider streams","Typed evidence is not a vote","Name and category evidence","Identity conflicts are returned upstream for review","Untrusted input boundary"]},{"slug":"crosswalks","title":"Reviewed crosswalks","text":"Reviewed mappings and review worklists A crosswalk row is a versioned, source-specific assertion about admissible taxonomy codes—not an opaque classification prediction. Five mutually distinct mapping kinds Mapping Meaning Codes EXACT The reviewed label supports this exact code. Exactly one. SUBTREE The label supports this code or an unspecified descendant. Exactly one root. UNION Admissible alternatives lie in multiple distinct subtrees. At least two nonredundant roots. NOT_ACTIVITY Source denotes a feature that is not a PSIC economic activity. None. UNCODEABLE Source category is too broad/semantically weak to code. None. Important: NOT_ACTIVITY means something different from an unknown or ambiguous business. UNCODEABLE is not an assertion that an economic activity does not exist. Neither may be converted to a code by a blind LCA. Bundled reviewed inventory PlaceType PH 0.1.2 carries 346 reviewed PSIC Rev. 5 entries , consisting of 249 SUBTREE , 45 EXACT , four UNION , 17 NOT_ACTIVITY , and 31 UNCODEABLE rows: 201 Overture and 145 OSM. The first 328 are the transferred reviewed set; eighteen were added after review of PSIC title-search results, and seven of those correct the search result. The 178-rule specialized advisory catalog is a different resource with a different authority level. The older 1,993-row worklist is not 1,993 accepted decisions. These counts describe reviewed rules , not the number of establishments correctly classified in a benchmark. A rule has scope A crosswalk identity includes source , source_value , source_field , scheme , and version . Matching uses match_type = exact | contains | regex . Normalization is performed consistently for literal rules; regex is compiled and validated separately. Conflicting duplicate exact rules fail validation. If overlapping contains/regex rules imply different decisions, the observed field is flagged as ambiguous and excluded from that field's accepted evidence (or made fatal with --fail-on-ambiguous-crosswalk ). Column Example Meaning source osm Source namespace. source_value shop=pharmacy Observed category label. source_field category Category or name matching. scheme / version psic / rev5 Statistical scope. mapping_kind SUBTREE Meaning of the assertion. codes 4772 The asserted root(s); ` match_type exact Literal/substring/regex semantics. The illustrative row above is not a recommendation to add a duplicate to the bundled rules: the package already loads reviewed PSIC Rev. 5 mappings by default. Worklist → suggestion → human review → accepted rule The crosswalk-init command enumerates observed vocabulary and frequency. crosswalk-suggest uses local lexical retrieval and review-status policies to produce candidate categories with reasons and scores. A suggestion is not a reviewed mapping; it must be promoted under the appropriate Express policy or explicitly adjudicated. The read-only reconciliation tool compares outside rule candidates to local reviewed states, reportable hierarchy relations, and specialized advisory evidence but never silently imports unreviewed authority. placetype crosswalk-init path\\to\\canonical_pois.parquet --scheme psic if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Worklist creation failed\" } The worklist normally orders category values by coverage so a reviewer can address frequently occurring observed labels first. Repeated runs preserve reviewed rows and refresh frequencies; absent reviewed categories are retained as zero-observation rows. Why review remains essential One OSM or Overture category can mean an activity, a physical structure, a product line, a facility name, or a broad venue. High lexical similarity between a source label and an official taxonomy title does not prove equivalence. The review process must choose the defensible subtree or abstain. Implementation: crosswalk.py · reviewed integration · reconciliation note .","headings":["Five mutually distinct mapping kinds","Bundled reviewed inventory","A rule has scope","Worklist → suggestion → human review → accepted rule","Why review remains essential"]},{"slug":"triangulation","title":"Evidence triangulation","text":"Evidence triangulation Triangulation here means comparing typed observations while respecting source dependence. More labels do not automatically mean more independent evidence. Start with the provenance graph Figure 1 — A provider record is not necessarily an independent observation. Overture can reuse Foursquare-origin information. A naive rule would count every provider field as another supporting vote. PlaceType PH instead assigns a dependency group to each SourceEvidence item and reasons over the admissible taxonomic subtrees . Foursquare and FSQ-derived Overture are one lineage; two categories from one Overture record are also dependent. Independent OSM and Overture statements can corroborate or contradict each other. Explore three controlled scenarios Worked source-evidence outcomes Select a case. This is an explanatory illustration of documented policy, not a live classifier or an accuracy estimate. Compatible Same lineage Conflict OSM shop=pharmacy Independent OSM lineage Overture pharmacy Independent Overture lineage Compatible — one supported PSIC branch Compatible reviewed mappings to the same subtree can support one code without a numerical confidence vote. The order of operations Parse source semantics without losing source identity ( osm key/value vs Overture primary/alternate/basic vs complete Foursquare hierarchy). Attach reviewed mapping objects or narrower trusted policy floors where permitted for PSIC Rev. 5. Group mapped evidence by provider lineage; dependent assertions may intersect or be flagged if disjoint. Intersect the admissible subtrees across independent groups. Compatible evidence supports the deepest asserted surviving root, not an inferred leaf. Report sibling-only backoff, unresolved union, semantic conflict, or eligibility conflict explicitly. Optional record-linkage warning fields turn some conflicts into REVIEW_ENTITY_MATCH . Triangulation does not mean majority voting Suppose FSQ and FSQ-derived Overture both suggest one activity while independent OSM asserts a disjoint activity. It is not two votes against one: FSQ and Overture are one dependency group. Counting them separately would manufacture false confidence. The classification engine can return CONFLICT rather than choosing the most popular label. The dependency grouping also explains why an Overture primary category and alternate category cannot be treated as two establishments. Their disagreement is potential within-source ambiguity , not independent evidence for the LCA. Name rules versus category rules A source's reviewed name rule and its reviewed category rule are dependent. A specific name rule can override a coarse incompatible source category, with a visible audit flag, but not by silently adding an extra independent vote. A reviewed exact category or an unrelated activity can block an administrative name-based correction into review. The classification chapter details these precedence policies. Distinguish a second kind of triangulation The joint PSIC/PCPC/PSCC peer-context recheck is a separate workflow from source fusion. It compares candidate rankings across independently prepared taxonomy proposals, but does not allow those other taxonomies to vote a PSIC code into existence. See cross-taxonomy recheck . Implementation: fusion.py · specialized/fusion.py · source-aware evidence note .","headings":["Start with the provenance graph","Explore three controlled scenarios","The order of operations","Triangulation does not mean majority voting","Name rules versus category rules","Distinguish a second kind of triangulation"]},{"slug":"fusion","title":"Tree fusion & backoff","text":"Taxonomy fusion and conservative backoff PlaceType PH fuses assertions as sets of admissible rooted subtrees. This preserves what reviewers actually claimed and prevents a single sparse taxonomy branch from creating unsupported specificity. The mathematical object Let a taxonomy be a rooted forest T = (V, E) with explicit parent edges. Let D(r) contain a root code r and all its descendants. Then a reviewed mapping denotes: EXACT(r) → a reviewed assertion selecting one code r ; the current fusion implementation still represents it as a rooted constraint , so it is not globally enforced as a singleton set during intersection; SUBTREE(r) → the admissible subtree D(r) , where the accepted reported code remains r until narrower evidence appears; UNION(r₁,…,rₖ) → the union of those rooted subtrees; NOT_ACTIVITY / UNCODEABLE → no coded subtree; eligibility policy handles them separately. The implementation uses normalize_roots() and intersect_subtrees() to operate on asserted roots without materializing every leaf. The EXACT / SUBTREE distinction remains meaningful in crosswalk validation and some policy gates, but the fusion operation currently handles both as rooted constraints; this is an important interpretation boundary, not a strict exact-code constraint solver. With compatible roots, the intersection preserves the descendant. With disjoint roots it is empty. Figure 1 — A broad division assertion and a more specific compatible group assertion can yield the group. A broad assertion alone must remain broad. Dependent groups and independent groups Within a dependency group, compatible constraints intersect. A dependent disagreement widens to the union of declared roots and adds DEPENDENT_CONFLICT:<group> ; the operational PSIC Rev. 5 classifier may then abstain explicitly. Across independent groups, disjoint admissible sets are a true semantic conflict; the implementation does not invent a common activity just to fill a field. A deliberately narrow sibling exception When independent PSIC evidence differs only between immediate sibling nodes, the package can back off exactly one level to their shared parent, provided all other asserted roots are compatible ancestors and that parent is below section level. 47111 source A ↘ 4711 shared parent ↗ 47112 source B Here the output may be parent 4711 with INDEPENDENT_SIBLING_BACKOFF . The same rule does not convert disagreement between unrelated divisions into a meaningless section-level answer. This is a specific implemented policy, not ordinary LCA applied to every conflict. Why leaf expansion is wrong Consider a partially loaded division whose only loaded descendant is one subclass. Mapping a label to that division says the label supports the division ; it does not say that the reviewer discovered the only descendant. Expanding to leaves and taking an LCA would incorrectly output a subclass. Operating on declared subtree roots preserves the epistemic ceiling of the evidence. Status semantics Fusion status Meaning Normal coding consequence EMPTY No coded mapping survived. No code; optional fallback may run. SINGLE One mapped evidence item. The asserted code is retained. NESTED Compatible evidence at different depths. Deepest supported asserted root. INTERSECT Intersecting compatible constraints; includes sibling backoff branch. Supported code or bounded backoff. UNION Several admissible branches remain. Candidate set and unresolved outcome where no single root is defensible. CONFLICT Independent assertions are disjoint. Abstain; preserve candidates and flags. The final classifier's status vocabulary is broader than FusionStatus : eligibility, compound sources, administrative decisions, LLM fallbacks and entity-match reviews can alter the returned status without changing the meaning of the fusion stage. Failure modes and alternatives rejected Majority vote: not used; dependent providers would be double counted. Arbitrary LCA: not used for incompatible independent branches; a common root can be too general to support one economic activity. Numeric prefix ancestry: not used; sections are letters and version changes can recode categories. Always choose longest code: not used; the longest match can be unsupported, or exact/union semantics may differ. Implementation: fusion.py · test_fusion.py .","headings":["The mathematical object","Dependent groups and independent groups","A deliberately narrow sibling exception","Why leaf expansion is wrong","Status semantics","Failure modes and alternatives rejected"]},{"slug":"joint-recheck","title":"Cross-taxonomy recheck","text":"Cross-taxonomy triangulation and bounded recheck The joint worklist aligns PSIC, PCPC, and PSCC proposals under the same source/category key—but the three schemes are not interchangeable votes. The peer recheck only tests how a *fixed candidate set* responds to admissible peer labels. Three classification questions, one observed source value joint_key is a stable digest of source, source field and source value, excluding taxonomy/version. Thus an observed Overture category can have separate PSIC, PCPC, and PSCC worklist rows with a shared key, retaining the distinct code meanings and review states. Figure 1 — The first-pass set is a control. Peer context may rerank candidates, never add codes not in the controlled shortlist. Pass 1 — Independent source-only retrieval Each taxonomy independently retrieves candidates using original source evidence . The local retriever uses a 0.6-weight word TF–IDF component and a 0.4-weight character n-gram TF–IDF component; its hierarchical pass first selects plausible coarse branches and then ranks within them. Codes from another taxonomy are not added as if they were source evidence. Accepted reviewed codes and eligible suggested_codes may later provide peer context. Raw unaccepted candidate_codes do not cross scheme boundaries. At most one version of each peer scheme contributes; reviewed rows take precedence over suggestions. Pass 2 — Bounded peer-context recheck For a target row, the recheck adds other schemes' titles , not bare numerical code tokens, to the same base query. The retriever is constrained to the first-pass candidate set . Therefore a peer code can change the ordering of existing possibilities but cannot manufacture a new PSIC category absent from the original retrieval. This is a consistency/sensitivity diagnostic, not an official correspondence between activity, product and commodity taxonomies. A bakery's principal activity and the products it sells can both be correctly classified while their code strings and taxonomy titles are unrelated. Recheck outcomes Recheck condition Reported status Meaning Top accepted candidate remains stable STABLE Peer context did not change its top code. Strongly different top candidate SHIFT Accepted mapping needs review. Change below configured margin SHIFT_WEAK Inconclusive; not a decisive contradiction. No comparable peers NO_PEERS No recheck was possible; not success. Missing control/recheck retrieval NO_CONTROL_HIT / NO_RECHECK_HIT No valid comparison. Candidate-only changes CANDIDATE_STABLE / CANDIDATE_SHIFT Diagnostics only; cannot authorize an accepted mapping. Missing peer taxonomy MISSING_TAXONOMY Diagnostic unavailable. PCPC sibling discrepancy COARSENED (when applicable) An automatic PCPC proposal can back off to a verified common parent; reviewed rules remain unchanged. A group-level RECHECK state is reserved for material shifts involving accepted evidence; candidate-only movement cannot escalate the worklist by itself. Why this is not ordinary triangulation by voting A stable peer-context result is not independent evidence that the selected code is true. The recheck sees labels derived from related classifications of one source value; they may be semantically related, correlated, or inappropriate for a different scheme. Stability is conditional on the first-pass candidate set and retrieval scoring. Worklist pipeline crosswalk-init → crosswalk-suggest → bounded recheck → reviewed/adopted mapping → classify . Suggestions and recheck outputs carry audit columns such as control_query , recheck_query , recheck_candidate_codes , recheck_top_code , recheck_margin , peer_context , and joint_status . The default batch size for first-pass retrieval is 256 unique queries ; repeated identical text is vectorized once per taxonomy, and source-specific branch restrictions still apply independently. These performance choices do not alter candidate semantics. Crucial limit: automatic promotion Express can promote a suggestion with no valid peer verdict by default; it labels it AUTO_ACCEPTED_UNCHECKED , not REVIEWED . --no-promote-unchecked holds these suggestions; --hold-inconclusive separately holds weak shifts. Never report default Express coverage as exclusively human-reviewed coverage. Implementation: joint_crosswalk.py · suggest.py · architecture note .","headings":["Three classification questions, one observed source value","Pass 1 — Independent source-only retrieval","Pass 2 — Bounded peer-context recheck","Recheck outcomes","Why this is not ordinary triangulation by voting","Worklist pipeline","Crucial limit: automatic promotion"]},{"slug":"classification","title":"Classification decisions","text":"Operational classification policy The classifier applies a sequence of explicit gates before returning a code. Review, negative evidence, dependent contradictions, and a defensible high-level answer all have distinct meanings. Decision path Figure 1 — Conceptual ordering; see source code for exact conditional precedence and status/flag construction. Map evidence. Match source/category and reviewed name rules, adding trusted Rev. 5 source floors where permitted. Fuse and test eligibility. Compute admissible code subtrees and test NOT_ACTIVITY and UNCODEABLE separately. Protect against semantic contradictions. Independent activity versus non-activity, multiple incompatible OSM primary tags, and dependent source conflicts can force abstention. Check narrow administrative function. A precise education/health administrative office may be assigned PSIC 84120 only if relevant reviewed activity evidence does not contraindicate it. Ownership does not decide this. Respect eligibility and entity matching. Return NOT_PSIC_ACTIVITY , UNCODEABLE , CONFLICT , or REVIEW_ENTITY_MATCH as appropriate. Return deterministic fusion when a sufficiently supported code exists; never force a leaf beyond the strongest admissible asserted root. Optional traversal. If no deterministic result resolves the case and an LLM backend is configured, use restricted taxonomy descent; an unsupported model answer cannot erase a defensible accepted code. Scope of the reviewed policy The 346 packaged rules load by default only for PSIC Rev. 5 . --no-reviewed-psic disables the new operational source interpretation, trusted floors, and administrative policy. Explicit custom crosswalks can remain active, so this comparison is a controlled policy change rather than a complete “no classification” mode. Other PSIC revisions do not inherit Rev. 5-specific trusted rules. For a place left with status EMPTY , the psic_search_* columns report a PSIC title search (the query plan, guards and thresholds of placetype suggest ), and a name-only place gets NAME_ONLY_CANDIDATES . The search never sets psic_code ; a category becomes coded only through a reviewed row. Status and audit fields Output Interpretation SINGLE , NESTED , INTERSECT A determinate outcome from mapped source fusion, with the code's supported hierarchy level. UNION A broader unresolved alternative set; inspect candidate codes. CONFLICT Disjoint activity assertions / failed compatibility. REVIEW_ENTITY_MATCH Semantic disagreement and upstream match-risk indicators. NOT_PSIC_ACTIVITY Source evidence establishes the feature is not an economic activity. UNCODEABLE Inadequate semantic resolution, different from a negative activity claim. EMPTY , REVIEW No supported code from the available components. LLM_PARTIAL , LLM_FULL , FUSION_BACKOFF Optional model traversal output or fallback; these require an LLM backend. POTENTIAL_PRODUCT_FAMILY_PARTIAL/FULL PCPC classification of a possible family, not a complete basket. NO_PRODUCT_EVIDENCE PSCC commodity-level policy gate. candidate_codes , evidence_sources , flags , deciding_component , audit , and classification_depth explain how the result arose. They should accompany any interpretation of coverage or an I–O projection. One source can be negative while another is coded The engine treats independent NOT_ACTIVITY versus coded activity as an explicit conflict rather than letting the coded source automatically win. By contrast, UNCODEABLE means “this category gives no sufficient code”; it does not negate an independent defensible exact mapping. Names, administration, ownership PSIC 84120 refers to public administration of health, education, and other social programmes ; the word “school” in an administrative office's OSM annotation does not by itself establish the actual service activity. The narrow administrative rule is a function classifier , not a government ownership classifier. Verified ownership evidence is handled later and separately. In particular, no high-level “public” label is allowed to bypass an exact reviewed PSIC mapping. Deterministic does not mean infallible The default --llm none avoids stochastic model calls and returns reproducible decisions, but rules and data can be wrong. They require empirical evaluation on independently adjudicated places with correct entity identity. Determinism is a software property, not a measurement of predictive validity. Implementation: classifier.py · reviewed_psic.py · models.py .","headings":["Decision path","Scope of the reviewed policy","Status and audit fields","One source can be negative while another is coded","Names, administration, ownership","Deterministic does not mean infallible"]},{"slug":"retrieval-llm","title":"Retrieval & optional LLM","text":"Retrieval and optional constrained LLM The model path is a fallback, not an alternative source of official codes. It retrieves plausible branches locally and asks a model to traverse only legal children of the installed taxonomy. Local lexical retrieval The retriever indexes official node title, description and inclusion text. Exclusion notes are not indexed as positive search text ; they are used as boundary evidence in traversal prompts. Two word representations are combined: word TF–IDF, unigrams and bigrams, sublinear term frequency, weight 0.6 ; character-boundary TF–IDF, 3–5-grams, weight 0.4 . For a query q and node v , the retrieval score is the weighted cosine-like TF–IDF dot product of the two representations. The retriever can select coarse level branches before ranking finer nodes, and it supports top_n , subtree restrictions, and batched queries. Repeated query strings are scored once per batch to reduce memory and repeated vectorization. A constrained tree traversal Figure 1 — Model decisions are checked against legal taxonomy children, not accepted as arbitrary generated codes. At each node, the optional backend receives only the current node and admissible children. Valid responses are one displayed code, STOP_HERE , or INSUFFICIENT in constrained JSON. STOP_HERE preserves a node supported by the evidence when it cannot distinguish children; INSUFFICIENT backs out of a node that is not itself supported, rather than falsely leaving it on the accepted path. The normal passes=3 cycles precision-, boundary- and evidence-focused prompt variants. A strict majority of pass paths selects the deepest common supported code; otherwise the result can be unresolved or back off. Changing the number of passes to a value not divisible by the number of variants is explicitly flagged as potentially unbalanced. Backends and caches The classify CLI supports --llm none , --llm hf and --llm ollama . Deterministic mode ( none ) is the default, including in express . Hosted or local model availability and API usage depend on the configured backend. No LLM weights or credentials are bundled with PlaceType PH. The decision cache's identity includes taxonomy version and content fingerprint, model/provider/base URL, prompt fingerprint, evidence, restrictions and pass count. This avoids reusing a decision from a materially changed prompt or model context. Safety and abstention The prompt explicitly treats establishment text as untrusted input and instructs the model not to follow instructions contained in place names, categories or products. Invalid child choices are not made into valid classification codes. An LLM cannot discard a reviewed deterministic code merely because a model refused a deeper branch. Scheme-specific boundaries A PCPC code inferred from a place type is a possible product/service family , never a complete product basket. A PSCC code cannot be generated from a place name alone; absent confirmed source mapping, it needs explicit product or commodity evidence to admit traversal. The three taxonomy questions cannot be collapsed into the same predictive target. Implementation: retrieval.py · traversal.py · cache.py .","headings":["Local lexical retrieval","A constrained tree traversal","Backends and caches","Safety and abstention","Scheme-specific boundaries"]},{"slug":"institutions","title":"Institutions & ownership","text":"Institutions, activity and ownership “What does this establishment do?” and “Who owns this institution?” are separate questions. The first is a PSIC activity problem; the second requires independent, attributable evidence and only affects narrowly eligible economic-industry candidate sets. Why separate the questions? A government education office does not deliver teaching in the same sense as a school; a public hospital and a private hospital can both carry the same PSIC health-service activity while falling into different public/private I–O industries. An institutional name, accreditation, participation list or source category alone does not establish legal ownership. Figure 1 — Activity is classified first. Ownership evidence may refine separate I–O candidate sets only after strong identity and mapping gates pass. Operational administrative function The Rev. 5 PSIC policy can recognize narrow administrative names such as a DepEd Schools Division Office and assign 84120 , provided incompatible reviewed activity evidence does not veto it. It does not infer public/private school ownership. Generic “Department of Health” or a frontline hospital/school must not be force-reassigned merely because a government department is mentioned. Specialized advisory evidence The separate 178-rule specialized catalog handles activity patterns, institution types, source-specific signals, and review candidates. It emits audit fields such as specialized_status , specialized_candidate_codes , administrative_candidate_code , ownership_candidate , registry evidence fields and specialized_audit . These advisory candidates do not silently overwrite accepted PSIC, PCPC or PSCC decisions. A source label suggesting “public” is not equal to registry verification. Explicit local registry references Institutional enrichment is enabled by default . The four bundled national datasets are CHED HEIDA (2,424 eligible records), a single PhilHealth Level 1–3 hospital registry (1,338), UniFAST (1,955), and DepEd (30,364). All 36,081 reference records load locally without a separate download or configuration. Ambiguous HEIDA records are excluded. Set PLACETYPE_PH_INSTITUTION_REFERENCES only to override with a validated local JSON configuration or use the literal off to disable the stage. Invalid configurations and corrupted bundled data fail closed. See docs/INSTITUTION_REGISTRY_TOOLS.md . { \"schema\": \"placetype-ph-institution-reference-config-v1\", \"references\": { \"verified_links\": \"C:\\\\data\\\\reviewed_institution_links.json\" } } This is only a configuration illustration: it does not assert that any particular record has been verified. Source/licensing checks and separate review of institution records are operator responsibilities. Evidence ladder and identity safeguards Evidence Identity/ownership interpretation Independently reviewed canonical-to-registry link Strong identity with auditable source and verification date; still subject to conflicts and activity compatibility. True official facility ID plus canonical name and locality Can support a strong exact site match under the resolver's constraints. Official directory row with name/city similarity Provisional, not a verified physical site. BEIS school-ID prefix, UniFAST capture row, publication-row identifier Hints/reference evidence; do not automatically prove branch identity or legal ownership. OSM/Overture owner/operator claim Explicit source claim, not independently verified ownership. Religious prefix / “National” in name Never sufficient alone to establish legal ownership. Wrong-site branches, incompatible PSIC domains, duplicate identities, or contradictory evidence force review or abstention. The packaged registry is available offline; no network download is required for default institutional enrichment. Exact gated I–O candidate refinement When strong institutional identity actually resolves ownership, ownership_io.py can append separate refined candidate columns for eligible education (PSIC division 85) or human health (division 86). The original I–O candidate sets are never overwritten. Activity division Public IO80 / IO240 Private IO80 / IO240 PSIC 85 education 74 / 229 75 / 230 PSIC 86 human health 76 / 231 77 / 232 The gate additionally requires a SINGLE PSIC result, eligible mapped division/group status, valid bridge basis, exact two-element public/private ambiguity, complete official reference provenance, and checked bundled numeric/name correspondence. Otherwise the refinement abstains. These are not default assignments for every school or clinic. Implementation: institutional_pipeline.py · ownership_io.py · institutional data guide .","headings":["Why separate the questions?","Operational administrative function","Specialized advisory evidence","Explicit local registry references","Evidence ladder and identity safeguards","Exact gated I–O candidate refinement"]},{"slug":"io-projection","title":"PSIC to I–O","text":"From PSIC activity to PSA I–O industries A classified activity is not automatically an observed supplier, transaction, or uniquely identified industry. PlaceType PH projects PSIC codes into **candidate sets** for the PSA 2018 input–output industry system, preserving revision and correspondence uncertainty. Why there are two bridges The package classifies establishments against PSIC Revision 5 , while the PSA 2018 input–output industries use the 2019 update to the 2009 PSIC . Therefore the correspondence is not a simple lookup of identical codes: Figure 1 — Two separately versioned reference assets produce candidate I–O sets. An ambiguous candidate set is preserved, not coerced to one industry. Choose the deepest section, division or group ancestor in Rev. 5 with a usable, title-compatible version-bridge row. Follow psic_rev5_to_psic_2019.csv to the corresponding PSIC 2019 code(s). Relation may be same , recoded , renamed , changed_scope , new , or no_counterpart . Combine the derived psic_2019_to_io_2018.csv rows into sets of IO16, IO80 and IO240 candidates. A revision bridge basis is code_title_match , draft , or reviewed . Preserve the candidate codes, names, confidence, map status, bridge basis, relation, and correspondence level in the classified summary. The concordance is a derived analytical reference , not an official PSA PSIC-to-I–O codebook; the bridge contains both reviewed and draft rows. See DATA_SOURCES.md . Exact candidate set versus map-ready code For each resolution, io16_codes , io80_codes and io240_codes hold a potentially multi-valued set. io*_map_code records a singleton candidate or a separately labelled resolver decision. SINGLETON_CANDIDATE describes cardinality, not empirical truth; AMBIGUOUS_SET means there is no single choice under that mapping. Map-ready coverage and policy-resolved coverage are different. Field Meaning io16_codes , io80_codes , io240_codes Entire candidate sets, ; separated. io16_map_code , io80_map_code , io240_map_code Singleton candidate or separately labelled resolver decision. io*_map_status Cardinality or resolver status; inspect before aggregation. io_mapping_status MAPPED_* , PROVISIONAL_* , or detailed unmapped/no-counterpart status. io_mapping_bridge_relation , io_mapping_bridge_basis How and on what basis the revisions were related. io_mapping_psic_level , io_mapping_psic_code The actual ancestor level used for the bridge. io*_confidence Metadata about the concordance evidence; not a calibrated prediction probability. The difference between draft and accepted correspondence A hand-written draft bridge yields PROVISIONAL_* when it changes the candidate sets. If an already accepted non-draft ancestor yields exactly the same candidate set, the output may instead cite that ancestor. A no_counterpart does not mean the activity was impossible in 2019; it means the reference cannot establish a defensible mapping for that category. A same-code/same-title code_title_match is generated evidence, not independently reviewed semantic equivalence. Rev. 5 scope changes must be handled explicitly (including the accommodation intermediation change identified in the bundled bridge documentation). For a reviewed UNION, I–O projection maps the admissible subtrees individually and unions their candidate sets, not their common ancestor. Incomplete UNION mappings abstain. The official IO240 → IO80 → IO16 hierarchy validates the concordance and constrains final codes. io_mapping_draft_levels records which levels depend on a draft bridge. Strict and evidence-weighted modes withhold those levels unless stronger permitted evidence establishes the code. A withheld singleton is PROVISIONAL_BRIDGE_NOT_RESOLVED , not ambiguous. none explicitly records that no level depends on the draft; blank provisional metadata is treated conservatively. Use --io-resolution-policy strict (default) for conservative resolution; evidence-weighted also permits direct tags within the candidate set and explicit source ownership; extended additionally permits labelled draft mappings, direct fallbacks, draft subgroup narrowing and ownership hints. Candidate sets remain unchanged. Inspect io*_resolved_code , io*_resolved_status and io*_resolved_source together; none is an accuracy certificate. Ownership narrowing is separate For narrowly eligible public/private education or human-health pairs, strongly verified institutional ownership can produce io80_refined_* and io240_refined_* columns. The original candidate sets and basic I–O mapping statuses remain unchanged; see Institutions . Interpretation boundary Mapping a restaurant into a candidate I–O industry does not identify its local suppliers, its input–output coefficients, its sales, or its geographic economic influence. It is a classification and correspondence layer ; downstream economic modeling must supply separate assumptions and data. Implementation: io_mapping.py · io80_resolver.py · reference documentation .","headings":["Why there are two bridges","Exact candidate set versus map-ready code","The difference between draft and accepted correspondence","Ownership narrowing is separate","Interpretation boundary"]},{"slug":"express","title":"Express workflow","text":"Express: the automatic end-to-end workflow `placetype express` is an orchestration layer over the existing taxonomy importer, joint worklist, suggestion/recheck, deterministic classifier, and GIS exporter. Its defaults are convenient; they are not equivalent to a fully adjudicated mapping inventory. The execution plan Figure 1 — Resumable execution. The package reuses completed work only when its cache identity says the dependencies have not changed. The pipeline generally performs these phases: verify input; acquire or reuse taxonomies; seed a joint category worklist; generate lexical suggestions; recheck with bounded cross-taxonomy context; report what was reviewed, promoted, held, or unresolved; classify using the resulting joint crosswalk; append I–O candidate sets; write a compact QGIS-ready GeoParquet. The four promotion states you must distinguish State in express_status Semantics REVIEWED Existing reviewed mapping preserved. AUTO_ACCEPTED Machine proposal cleared by an available peer recheck. AUTO_ACCEPTED_INCONCLUSIVE Peer recheck was weak/inconclusive but policy allowed promotion. AUTO_ACCEPTED_UNCHECKED No usable recheck verdict; default policy still promoted the suggestion. Held states include HELD_RECHECK , HELD_INCONCLUSIVE , and HELD_NO_VERDICT . UNRESOLVED remains without an adopted code. COARSENED can produce a narrowly checked PCPC sibling-parent backoff for automatic suggestions; it does not override reviewed human mappings. The default promotion policy Express defaults to --promote-unchecked and does not hold weak inconclusive rechecks unless requested. This maximizes useful initial coverage while explicitly labeling unverified promotions. It is not the conservative setting for a scientific accuracy benchmark. Use --no-promote-unchecked to hold no-verdict suggestions and --hold-inconclusive to hold weak shifts separately. A one-scheme run has no peer taxonomy to compare with and so may produce a large number of unchecked suggestions; the CLI warns about this. $places = \"..\\openplaces-ph\\data\\output\\areas_metro_manila\\canonical_pois.parquet\" placetype express $places --workers 1 --hold-inconclusive if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Express failed\" } Cache identity and reproducibility Express computes its run key from the OpenPlaces input state, selected schemes, package version, taxonomy fingerprints, reviewed worklist states, product-column selection, promotion policies, retrieval/classifier tuning, I–O resolver policy and content fingerprints of the bundled reviewed PSIC CSV, the version bridge, the concordance, official hierarchy, subgroup refinement table and direct I–O rules. The selected resolution policy and full content hashes of the selected bundled manifest or custom institutional configuration and all active reference files are part of the key; the semantic cache version is joint-v9.4.6-bundled-national-registry . Choose placetype express $places --io-resolution-policy extended for exploratory coverage with labelled provisional evidence, or omit the option for strict mode. Use different --output paths to preserve separate final GIS exports. The console reports actual resolved coverage and withheld provisional singletons separately from candidate/map-ready coverage. Inputs under 8 MiB use a content hash; larger inputs use file size and modification time as a cheaper identity. This is a performance trade-off: timestamp/size identity is less robust to adversarial or unusual in-place changes. Completed runs are checked against manifest and required output files/schema before reuse; this does not independently revalidate empirical accuracy. Where Express writes data Temporary worklist state lives in data/work/express/<cache-key>/ ; reusable classification runs live in output/express/<cache-key>/ . The default final GIS output is output/<input-scope>_placetype.parquet . Express does not modify the upstream OpenPlaces Parquet. When not to use Express For controlled comparison of the reviewed deterministic PSIC policy, use placetype classify --schemes psic --llm none directly. That isolates the reviewed rule inventory and avoids accidental promotion of machine guesses. For model-based classification on unresolved cases, the lower-level classify command offers explicit LLM settings. Implementation: express.py · cli.py .","headings":["The execution plan","The four promotion states you must distinguish","The default promotion policy","Cache identity and reproducibility","Where Express writes data","When not to use Express"]},{"slug":"outputs","title":"Outputs & GIS","text":"Artifacts, schemas and GIS PlaceType PH publishes both an audit-rich result table and a compact map-ready view. Neither should be confused with ground truth: every code remains scoped to a scheme, statistical version, and evidence policy. entity_classifications.parquet One row per canonical_id × requested taxonomy. Core columns include scheme , version , code , level , status , deciding_component , candidate_codes , evidence_sources , flags , audit , model , traversal_agreement , classification_depth , branch_max_depth , and max_depth . List/audit fields are JSON strings in the Parquet table. This is the primary dataset for studying a classifier's decisions . A missing code may be principled ( NOT_PSIC_ACTIVITY , UNCODEABLE , CONFLICT ) or simply uncovered ( EMPTY ); do not collapse all blank codes into an error category. classified_pois.parquet One row per canonical place, preserving available geometry/location and convenience fields ( psic_code , psic_level , psic_status , and equivalents for other requested schemes). It additionally holds derived I–O industry candidate sets, role evidence, and optional specialized/institutional fields. When GeoParquet metadata exists, the pipeline attempts to preserve it; the manifest reports preservation or failure explicitly. Important: io80_codes = \"74; 75\" means one of two candidate industries, not two simultaneously observed industries. A singleton map code or a labelled resolver decision is distinct from a policy-resolved code. See PSIC to I–O . The detailed classification table includes JSON admissible_roots ; the place summary includes psic_admissible_roots , io_mapping_draft_levels , draft subgroup sets, direct I–O evidence, ownership inferences and io*_resolved_code , io*_resolved_status , io*_resolved_source . These resolved columns are also available in GIS export. Candidate, refined, inferred and resolved values are not interchangeable. Two review groups are added: psic_search_* (PSIC title search for places without a code; never sets psic_code ) and institution_psic_proposal_* (the public or private PSIC subtree implied by a known ownership side; diagnostic only). run.json manifest io_mapping.resolution records the selected policy, implementation policy, rule fingerprint and per-level coded-row, status and source counts. Coverage is not a measure of classification accuracy. Each run identifies package version, source path, selected schemes and versions, taxonomy fingerprints, active reviewed crosswalk fingerprints, mapping ambiguity counts, LLM prompt/model metadata when applicable, I–O reference provenance and status counts, and output file names. Input reference hashes allow some material changes to be detected; they do not attest the source's factual accuracy. GIS export The separate placetype gis-export command produces a compact GeoParquet file for QGIS. It exports string-typed assigned codes and the actual official ancestor codes for each level: psic_section , psic_division , psic_group , psic_class , psic_subclass ; analogous level columns exist for PCPC and PSCC. A code assigned at division or group level leaves more-specific fields blank , rather than filling them with an invented subclass. The output can also carry I–O code sets, singleton map fields, map status and provenance—but omits bulky name/audit fields by design. placetype gis-export output\\iloilo-reviewed if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"GIS export failed\" } GeoParquet and fingerprint safeguards The exporter rejects an invalid/missing geometry, invalid classification codes, or taxonomy fingerprint drift by default. It rewrites the GeoParquet metadata so references to omitted covering/bounding-box columns are not left dangling, and records both source-run and export-time provenance. Do not disable a taxonomy fingerprint check as an ordinary convenience; this override changes the interpretation contract. Geospatial accuracy is inherited, not generated The coordinates, canonical entity geometry, source lineage and record-linkage uncertainty originate in OpenPlaces. PlaceType PH does not improve geocoding, triangulate points, route roads, or create network partitions. Its map export is a representation of existing classification results. Performance profile For deterministic --llm none , the pipeline supports --workers N spawn-safe process workers and chunked row dictionary conversion. It still materializes the entire input DataFrame and entire result table: this is not bounded-memory streaming Parquet I/O . Large national runs may need enough RAM or a future streaming implementation. Parallel worker count must not be used with a live LLM backend in the current CLI. Implementation: pipeline.py · gis.py .","headings":["entity_classifications.parquet","classified_pois.parquet","run.json manifest","GIS export","GeoParquet and fingerprint safeguards","Geospatial accuracy is inherited, not generated","Performance profile"]},{"slug":"evaluation","title":"Validation & evaluation","text":"Validation, gold labels and accuracy Passing software tests confirms invariants and expected decisions on fixtures. It does not establish that a source-category rule is correct for the general Philippine establishment population. Four different validation questions Question Evidence required Already covered? Does the code execute consistently? CI and deterministic regression tests. Yes, for tested paths and Python versions. Does the taxonomy preserve its published hierarchy? Official-source counts and import validation. PSIC Rev. 5 has specific structural gates; PCPC/PSCC require source-specific checks. Does the rule assign the correct category for a real place? Independent adjudicated establishment labels and identity verification. Not established by CI alone. Does a PSIC or I–O singleton correspond to actual economic output? Verified concordance and relevant external economic evidence. Not established by a mapping alone. Construct an independent gold set Sample canonical entities across source combinations, rule types, classification depths, statuses ( SINGLE , INTERSECT , UNION , CONFLICT , UNCODEABLE , NOT_PSIC_ACTIVITY ), location, establishment size/category, and higher-risk entity-match indicators. Preserve a random component for population-rate estimation; oversampling difficult cases without weights is useful for diagnostics but cannot directly estimate overall population accuracy. Adjudicators should verify the actual site identity and principal economic activity against the relevant official taxonomy revision , independently of the classifier's proposed code. Label negative cases explicitly instead of silently dropping them from evaluation. Gold file schema At minimum supply canonical_id , scheme , and gold_code , with optional gold_status : gold_status gold_code Meaning CODED Valid code Activity/product/commodity reference established. NOT_CODEABLE Blank Evidence insufficient for an admissible taxonomy code. NOT_PSIC_ACTIVITY Blank Physical feature is not a PSIC economic activity. NON_ECONOMIC_POI Blank Legacy alias accepted by evaluator. Invalid codes, missing required labels and contradictory negative statuses are fatal rather than being removed from the denominator. Run the evaluator placetype evaluate output\\iloilo-reviewed\\entity_classifications.parquet ` gold.csv --scheme psic --output-dir output\\evaluation\\reviewed if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw \"Evaluation failed\" } The evaluator reports per-depth production rate and accuracy , Cohen's kappa, exact-code accuracy, hierarchy-compatible accuracy (including honest ancestor backoff), over-specificity, wrong-branch outcomes, mean tree distance, unknown prediction codes, and code-avoidance on negative gold cases. One division-level classification counts as produced at its supported depth, not as an invented subclass. Compare reviewed and legacy policies Use the same OpenPlaces input and verified taxonomy. Run reviewed deterministic classification and legacy --no-reviewed-psic to separate the reviewed rule-policy change. Compare exact/compatible accuracy, abstention, false-positive code rate, coverage, source-specific error patterns and status distribution. A coverage gain that lowers precision is not automatically a scientific improvement. For Express, stratify by review source : REVIEWED , AUTO_ACCEPTED , AUTO_ACCEPTED_INCONCLUSIVE , and AUTO_ACCEPTED_UNCHECKED must be reported separately. Default Express promotion does not create independently validated labels. Evaluation limitations A convenience 50- or 100-row CLI slice is a smoke test, not a representative evaluation. Human label agreement, ambiguous PSIC scope, entity-linkage failures, selected cities versus national coverage and temporal changes in source categories are all material uncertainties. Record sampling scheme, adjudication source/date, disagreements, and negative labels so the benchmark is reproducible without redistributing restricted raw registry data. Implementation: evaluate.py · tests/test_evaluate.py .","headings":["Four different validation questions","Construct an independent gold set","Gold file schema","Run the evaluator","Compare reviewed and legacy policies","Evaluation limitations"]},{"slug":"reproducibility","title":"Reproducibility","text":"Reproducibility, caching and safe publication A reproducible classification is one whose code revision, taxonomy revision, reviewed mappings, source evidence, decision policy, and output can be identified. Reproducing the computation is distinct from showing that its assumptions are true. Inputs that define a run canonical_pois.parquet : canonical IDs and observed provider evidence; geometry and upstream matching uncertainty remain part of the source contract. Official taxonomy: scheme, version, normalized node content, explicit ancestry and fingerprint. Crosswalk: version-scoped reviewed rules and any explicit user paths, recorded with a stable content-based fingerprint. Policy: reviewed PSIC operational mode, deterministic/traversal settings, accepted source-floor behavior, administrative gates, and eligible specialized enrichment. I–O references: packaged concordance/bridge hashes, provisional versus reviewed relation and mapping statuses. Optional model: provider/base URL, model name, prompt fingerprint, pass count, input/restriction identity. run.json versus cache identity The classifier's run manifest records source/input path, package version, taxonomy fingerprints, active crosswalk fingerprint, LLM metadata, classification counts and I–O provenance. Express has a separate work-cache identity with the key semantic parameters; a cache hit means the requested computation's recorded dependencies match the cache recipe, not that the resulting economic interpretation has been independently validated. The current Express cache version is joint-v9.3-reviewed-psic-rev5 . Its pipeline state includes the SHA-256-derived file state of the packaged reviewed CSV. Earlier pre-integration cache keys are invalidated without deleting historical outputs. For small files, file_state hashes contents; large input files above 8 MiB use size/mtime. The latter is not a tamper-proof content identity: a same-size/same-timestamp replacement can escape detection. A scientific archive should retain independent source hashes for any input that must be authenticated byte-for-byte. Reviewed rules versus suggestions REVIEWED and accepted bundled mappings have stronger authority than AUTO_ACCEPTED_UNCHECKED . A crosswalk fingerprint proves which rules were loaded , not that the rules' empirical precision is high. The specialized rule catalog has its own fingerprint: v0.1.2 currently reports 178 advisory rules, separate from the 328 accepted PSIC inventory. Publication is not fully transactional The current classification pipeline writes entity_classifications.parquet before every optional enrichment and validation step has completed. If later institutional reference processing fails, the output directory can contain intermediate files that are not a complete successful run . Avoid treating the presence of Parquet files alone as an acceptance certificate. Check command success, a complete run.json with the declared outputs, and any required schema/provenance values. express checks key output names and schema before reuse, but publication-directory atomicity remains an explicit limitation. The docs website itself is just static content; deploying it does not publish any establishment dataset or optional institution register. Deterministic parallelism With --llm none , the pipeline supports spawn-based worker processes, merges worker diagnostics, and preserves result order. Chunked dictionary conversion reduces per-row Python overhead, but the full DataFrame and results are still materialized. Backend-driven traversal is not guaranteed deterministic across model deployments, even if code and prompts are identical. Deployment and branch safety The project's main is protected by required Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 checks, no force-push and a PR requirement. Documentation contributions should also pass link/build checks before merge. GitHub Pages deployment is a separate publication step: enable Deploy from a branch → main → /docs in Settings → Pages after the reviewed PR merges. A private institution dataset is never an input to this static build. Evidence lineage and references The decision register lists exactly which parts derive from a known statistical hierarchy or algorithm and which are package policy. Read the reference data source guide before republishing PSA source material or institutional extracts; the website intentionally ships no third-party raw registry data. Implementation: express.py · pipeline.py .","headings":["Inputs that define a run","run.json versus cache identity","Reviewed rules versus suggestions","Publication is not fully transactional","Deterministic parallelism","Deployment and branch safety","Evidence lineage and references"]},{"slug":"api-cli","title":"CLI & Python API","text":"CLI and Python API reference The public interface has a few stable entry points and a larger set of specialized review commands. Use the CLI for reproducible runs and import the core classes for controlled programmatic classification. Primary CLI commands Command Responsibility placetype version Print installed package version. placetype inspect PATH --top 30 Inspect observed source vocabulary and frequency. placetype taxonomy diagnose psic Diagnose official source before accepting a normalized reference. placetype taxonomy fetch psic Obtain/reuse official reference and write normalized taxonomy. placetype taxonomy validate PATH Check structure and hierarchy integrity. placetype crosswalk-init PATH --scheme psic Enumerate category worklist. placetype crosswalk-suggest PATH Suggest taxonomy candidates and run joint recheck where configured. placetype classify PATH --schemes psic --llm none Apply accepted crosswalks and deterministic policies. placetype express PATH Orchestrate joint classification and GIS export. placetype gis-export RUN_DIR Export compact QGIS GeoParquet. placetype evaluate PREDICTIONS GOLD --scheme psic Compare to independently adjudicated codes. Use placetype <command> --help to inspect the precise options for your installed version. Flag names and defaults here describe the verified v0.1.2 source tree. Important classification switches Option Default Effect --schemes psic,pcpc,pscc Comma-separated independent taxonomies. --io-resolution-policy strict Both classify and express accept strict, evidence-weighted or extended. See I–O projection for evidence gates. The Python pipeline uses io_resolution_policy . --reviewed-psic / --no-reviewed-psic Enabled Bundled accepted Rev. 5 policy or controlled legacy mode. --crosswalk PATH None Repeat to add explicit user mappings. --llm none none , hf , or ollama traversal backend. --passes 3 Traversal consensus passes (when LLM enabled). --product-column FIELD None Optional explicit product/commodity text for PCPC/PSCC. --workers 1 Deterministic spawn-based parallelism (no live LLM). --fail-on-ambiguous-crosswalk Disabled Treat observed scanned-rule conflicts as fatal. --limit None Pilot on first N rows; not a random evaluation sample. Python API: reviewed PSIC from placetype_ph.classifier import EntityClassifier from placetype_ph.crosswalk import Crosswalk from placetype_ph.reviewed_psic import bundled_psic_crosswalk_path from placetype_ph.taxonomy import Taxonomy psic_taxonomy = Taxonomy.load(\"reference/psic_rev5/nodes.parquet\") if psic_taxonomy.scheme != \"psic\" or psic_taxonomy.version != \"rev5\": raise ValueError(\"Expected a validated PSIC Rev. 5 taxonomy\") crosswalk = Crosswalk.load([bundled_psic_crosswalk_path()]) classifier = EntityClassifier(psic_taxonomy, crosswalk) result = classifier.classify_row({ \"canonical_id\": \"illustrative-id\", \"overture_category\": \"pharmacy\", }) print(result.code, result.status, result.flags) The snippet loads the normalized taxonomy file from the repository reference directory; verify it independently with placetype taxonomy validate before using it. For a legacy test, use EntityClassifier(psic_taxonomy, crosswalk, reviewed_psic_policy=False) and pass only the explicit crosswalks you wish to retain. Python API: data pipeline classify_openplaces(input_path, classifiers, output_dir, *, product_column=None, limit=None, workers=1, role_crosswalk=None, io_resolution_policy=\"strict\") processes canonical Parquet input and returns the two produced paths. For a multi-scheme run, supply a dictionary of scheme → EntityClassifier objects built from their own matching taxonomies; never reuse a PSIC taxonomy for PCPC or PSCC. Specialized inspection and review The modules under placetype_ph.specialized provide validation, evidence extraction, candidate-only rule reconciliation, institutional preview and optional enrichment. See the repository's specialized evidence guide and Priority 2 reconciliation instructions before running those commands with external references. Input and output contracts For exact columns, see Source evidence and Outputs . A missing canonical_id , invalid gold codes, conflicting exact crosswalk keys, an incomplete taxonomy, or an invalid opt-in institutional configuration should fail rather than yielding a plausible-looking partial classification. Source: cli.py · pipeline.py .","headings":["Primary CLI commands","Important classification switches","Python API: reviewed PSIC","Python API: data pipeline","Specialized inspection and review","Input and output contracts"]},{"slug":"decision-register","title":"Design decisions","text":"Method lineage and design decision register The purpose of this register is to state *why* each computational choice exists, what the implementation actually does, what alternative was rejected, and what evidence would be needed to validate it. Foundations versus package policy Component Foundation PlaceType PH implementation choice / trade-off Statistical classification PSA's official PSIC, PCPC and PSCC classifications Use versioned explicit parent graphs, strict import diagnostics and source fingerprints instead of numeric prefix assumptions. Source annotations Provider-typed observational records Keep OSM key=value , Overture structured categories, FSQ category hierarchy, and their provenance groups. Crosswalk matching Deterministic label-to-category rules Exact, contains and regex with validation; preserve EXACT vs SUBTREE vs UNION vs terminal policy. The present fusion engine still treats EXACT as a rooted constraint. Hierarchical fusion Intersections of rooted subtrees Fuse declared roots without leaf expansion; same-lineage dependencies cannot create independent votes. Conflict backoff Tree ancestry / least common ancestor Only one-level immediate sibling backoff below section for specific PSIC independent discrepancies; otherwise abstain. Category suggestions Lexical TF–IDF Combine word and character similarity (0.6/0.4), coarse branch selection, bounded batches; retrieval score is not truth probability. Joint taxonomy review Controlled reranking Restrict peer rerank to first-pass candidate set; peer titles only, never new cross-taxonomy code discovery. Automatic adoption Convenience workflow choice Express promotes no-verdict suggestions by default with audit status ; conservative operators can hold them. Optional LLM Hierarchical classification and constrained decoding Legal-child traversal, STOP_HERE , INSUFFICIENT , multi-pass consensus and cached prompt identity. Administrative function PSIC Rev. 5 activity distinction Narrow 84120 office correction with exact/unrelated evidence vetoes; ownership separately adjudicated. Institution identity Verified linking and source attribution Opt-in references, exact official site identity constraints, provisional name matches never silently promoted. I–O concordance PSA 2018 I–O industrial system Derived PSIC 2019 concordance and separate Rev. 5 bridge; candidate sets with provisional status and confidence. Map publication GeoParquet standard and taxonomy hierarchy Preserve geometry and actual ancestor paths; fail on schema/taxonomy drift. Evaluation Hierarchical classification metrics Report code-production rate separately from exact/hierarchy-compatible correctness and negative code avoidance. Reproducibility Content fingerprints and deterministic cache recipes Version-scoped rule hashes; cheaper size/mtime for large input; not full publication-directory atomicity yet. Design constraints and what they rule out Why no single numeric classifier confidence? Source crosswalk status, model path agreement, I–O concordance confidence and external identity evidence have different meanings . A single number would conflate independent and dependent sources, product versus activity semantics, and calibrated versus uncalibrated assertions. Why not classify products from the establishment category? An establishment may sell many products. PCPC permits only a potential family without direct product evidence; PSCC is more restrictive and requires explicit commodity text or accepted mapping. Inventing a product basket from a shop category would encode an unsupported economic model. Why no arbitrary cross-taxonomy voting? PSIC, PCPC, and PSCC answer different official classification questions. Joint peer recheck tests the sensitivity of an already retrieved candidate set , not the correctness of a third taxonomy's code. The bounded design avoids introducing entirely new candidates from contextual labels. Why preserve I–O ambiguity? A code set describes alternatives in a derived correspondence. A map-ready singleton merely says the candidate set currently has one value; there is no observed local buyer–supplier transaction evidence here. Users can accept only those candidate statuses appropriate for their downstream research. Why separate data publication from code reproducibility? A complete run.json and unchanged fingerprints identify computation. They do not validate individual establishments or grant permission to redistribute third-party registry data. The public documentation site contains only synthetic examples and code/algorithm exposition. Explicit remaining engineering trade-offs The full input/result materialization limits RAM; optional institutional enrichment is not publication-atomic; Express's large input identity is size/mtime; a final published accuracy claim requires a representative adjudicated benchmark; official PCPC/PSCC normalization counts require source-specific verification. See Limits . Read with: Architecture · Reproducibility · Evaluation .","headings":["Foundations versus package policy","Design constraints and what they rule out","Why no single numeric classifier confidence?","Why not classify products from the establishment category?","Why no arbitrary cross-taxonomy voting?","Why preserve I–O ambiguity?","Why separate data publication from code reproducibility?","Explicit remaining engineering trade-offs"]},{"slug":"limitations","title":"Limits & interpretation","text":"Scope, limitations and interpretation The package makes defensible, reproducible classification decisions under its explicit rules. It does not turn incomplete source metadata into observed economic transactions, site-verified institutional identity, or population-level accuracy guarantees. Scientific interpretation limits Principal activity is not revenue share. PSIC classification identifies an activity category, not turnover, jobs, gross value added, production functions, prices, or transactions. A source category is not an audited establishment record. OSM, Overture and FSQ differ in completeness, taxonomy vocabulary and update cadence; matching/lineage errors can persist in canonical records. Dependent labels are not independent confirmations. FSQ-derived Overture tags belong to the same source lineage; exact repeated labels do not establish probability or certainty. PCPC is not a complete production basket. Place-only PCPC family assignments require additional product data for stronger claims. PSCC is not an inference from a shop name. Traded commodities demand specific evidence; missing commodity text often implies abstention. I–O codes are candidates. A derived concordance and a singleton candidate are not proof of actual local supply-chain relationships. Institutional identity is site-specific. Name/city similarity, participation/accreditation, administrative jurisdiction, and religious name patterns do not prove legal ownership or physical branch equivalence. Cross-taxonomy recheck is not a gold label. A stable lexical rerank from peer titles is a diagnostic, not an independent statistical verification. Computational limits The input and result DataFrames are held in memory even though row conversion is chunked; true bounded-memory national-scale streaming remains open. Reviewed EXACT and SUBTREE have different stated rule meanings, but the current fusion implementation represents both as rooted constraints; exact singleton semantics are not globally enforced during fusion. This should be considered when auditing mixed evidence. The default deterministic path is reproducible under fixed inputs and rule code; an optional external LLM can introduce backend nondeterminism despite cached prompt identity. classification_run_ready requires manifests and output files/schema, but the pipeline may leave an intermediate classification Parquet after a later optional enrichment error. No all-or-nothing publication guarantee yet. Express hashes small input contents but uses size and modification time for large files. That cache identity is a performance optimization, not an archival integrity proof. GitHub Pages is documentation only . It does not deploy Python classification, user-supplied data, institution registries or OpenPlaces output. Data provenance and licensing Official PSA statistical definitions are cited in the repository's source guide ; normalized/derived tables may carry separate attribution and scope requirements. The package's MIT license is not permission to redistribute third-party institutional extracts. This documentation includes no institutional source records or proprietary downstream datasets. What still needs empirical work A stratified, independent, version-aware adjudication set should estimate precision, false positives, coverage, correct ancestor backoff, and error by source/provider and decision path. Comparisons must distinguish reviewed mappings from automatically promoted suggestions and preserve sampling weights where difficult cases were oversampled. A strong engineering result is still only an implementation result . The research claim becomes stronger when tested against ground truth independent of the classifier. Not part of PlaceType PH Road networks, shortest-path routing, network HDBSCAN, network Voronoi, economic centrality and geometric Delaunay triangulation are different algorithms. PlaceType PH's triangulation refers to semantic evidence comparison and bounded peer-taxonomy review. No geometric partition or clustering stage is hidden in this package. Next: Evaluation · Reference sources .","headings":["Scientific interpretation limits","Computational limits","Data provenance and licensing","What still needs empirical work","Not part of PlaceType PH"]},{"slug":"glossary","title":"Glossary & references","text":"Glossary, notation and sources A compact vocabulary for distinguishing observational records, statistical code semantics, review states, and downstream industrial interpretations. Glossary Term Meaning Canonical entity One OpenPlaces record after upstream provider reconciliation, identified by canonical_id . Source evidence Typed provider category/name observation with its own provenance and dependency group. Dependency group A set of statements sharing an upstream lineage, not independent confirmations. Crosswalk Versioned source-field rule mapping to a code/subtree/union or terminal decision. EXACT Human-reviewed assertion of one specific code. SUBTREE Assertion that the true category is in a root's subtree; the root limits reported specificity. UNION Multiple admissible taxonomy branches. NOT_ACTIVITY Source feature is not an economic activity for PSIC. UNCODEABLE Source observation cannot support a taxonomy code; not the same as non-economic. Sibling backoff Specific policy of moving one level to an immediate common parent for compatible narrow PSIC disagreements. Peer recheck Bounded sensitivity test of first-pass candidate ranking using labels from other taxonomies. Reviewed rule Explicitly accepted source-to-taxonomy decision, distinct from a machine suggestion. Automatic unchecked Suggestion promoted under Express default despite no usable peer verdict. Taxonomy fingerprint Stable content identity of the normalized hierarchy. Crosswalk fingerprint Stable content identity of the active reviewed rules used in a run. I–O candidate set Possible corresponding industries under a derived PSIC/PSA I–O bridge; not multiple observed activities. Map-ready singleton One candidate code at a resolution, not an external truth certificate. Verified institutional link Separately adjudicated canonical-to-registry identity evidence with source and date. run.json Manifest recording classifier, source version, taxonomy, crosswalk, reference and output metadata. Method references The principal theoretical and data sources are official statistical classification systems , explicit tree ancestry and set operations, standard TF–IDF retrieval, and conventional hierarchical validation metrics. The package's thresholds, corpus rules, source-floor coverage, sibling backoff and promotion decisions are documented implementation policies rather than attributed to an unrelated paper. Philippine Statistics Authority — PSIC classification Philippine Statistics Authority — PCPC classification Philippine Statistics Authority — PSCC classification PSA — 2018 input–output tables PlaceType PH official source catalog and licensing Source code and regression tests OpenPlaces PH upstream canonical entities Which page answers which question? Question Read Why does a place stop at a division? Fusion and backoff Why don't two sources count as two votes? Evidence triangulation Can a peer PCPC code prove a PSIC activity? Cross-taxonomy recheck Why is a government school office 84120? Classification and Institutions Why do I–O mappings have multiple codes? I–O projection How do I reproduce a run? Reproducibility How do I establish accuracy? Evaluation Documentation revision This guide describes the PlaceType PH **v0.1.2** source architecture verified on `main` after the reviewed PSIC integration and hardening PRs. When implementation semantics or official source revisions change, update the website and its tests together.","headings":["Glossary","Method references","Which page answers which question?"]}];
